/-!
Root import for the formalization of all main results in Chapter 3.
The regular compact-type Perron--Wright theorem and the annealed compact
uniform local factorial asymptotic are complete. Further modules prove
actual graph laws, profile and mark estimates, point-measure foundations,
and constructive type counts. Actual unmarked and empirical-mark
fixed-window point laws now have proved unique weak limits, with canonical
Perron marking; both starred windows are transported exactly. All finite
families of compactly supported global tests also have unique weak limiting
laws. Global unmarked point-process laws have proved full-sequence weak
convergence to a genuinely constructed unique vague-Borel probability law.
The actual starred unmarked global laws are transported by their literal
positive size dilation. A continuous real Brownian process is constructed
on an explicit countable Gaussian probability space, with all real finite-
dimensional laws and independent increments proved. The entire finite
irreducible enumeration branch is complete, including trees and common
bounded-surplus radius and Gaussian formulas. Actual global empirical-marked
laws converge to the canonical Perron marking of the genuine unmarked limit;
their literal starred rescaling is proved. Brownian paths and reflection
have genuinely measurable path-valued laws. Actual interval-area rates,
their unit planar intensity identity, and a countable independent Poisson
marking kernel are constructed. Actual clipped Brownian excursion
components have measurable endpoints and actual component integral areas,
with a proved countable nonrepeating rational parametrization. Literal
irreducible finite models have genuine uniform profile concentration and
the exact deterministic-type factorial isolation formula, now factored
into literal connected-graph edge-odds enumerators. A finite spatial
Poisson iid-atom law and its exact measurable-test Laplace functional are
constructed for every actual finite intensity, including the literal
unit planar intensity under each bounded reflected path. Genuine joint
Brownian-source/spatial laws retain the actual driver. Disjoint Borel-cell
counts have the proved independent Poisson law; actual clipped excursion
spatial counts, jointly with the actual Brownian source, are identified
with the entire countable area-rate marking law. Genuine full-horizon
Brownian subquadratic growth and parabolic drift to minus infinity are
proved simultaneously for every scalar drift parameter. The deterministic finite
enumeration prefactor has its actual uniform critical-window Gaussian
limit, including literal floor sizes. Literal finite population depletion
and rounding errors and actual Pearson-profile exponential averages are proved.
Actual isolation exponential fluctuations converge to one in L1, and
literal edge-odds corrections are uniformly negligible in actual product
laws. Actual full-horizon Brownian excursions have finite zero-ended
intervals, a measurable nonrepeating rational section, genuine measurable
areas, and exact eventual stabilization in bounded windows. Their full-area
conditional Poisson marking law has genuine source/path joint realizations,
all mixed factorial moments and exact finite-coordinate window consistency.
An actual independent spatial-atom family on all unit strips has a measurable
summed, almost-surely sigma-finite random measure and the exact full under-graph
intensity. Its actual bounded-window disjoint cell counts have the independent
Poisson law, and the whole actual full-excursion count family, jointly with
the genuine Brownian source, equals the full-area conditional marking law.
Its exact Laplace formula for every measurable NNReal test supported in a
bounded time window is proved, including the genuine path/source joint
integrals and exact agreement with the bounded sampler. The complete
literal deterministic finite local-factorial asymptotic is proved, including
arbitrary O(1)-rounded counts, whole critical windows, all bounded surplus,
raw paper time and actual floors; no B2/primitivity assumption is added.
Actual deterministic finite marked factorial expectations also converge
uniformly for every continuous coupled mark test to the density times
the genuine canonical Perron mark evaluation.
Their actual compact-window factorial moments and unique component-number
law limit are proved. Actual finite point laws are tight, and global
vague-law subsequential limits are constructed. Actual joint disjoint-cell
factorial limits, Boolean overlapping-query refinements and model-derived
boundary nullity prove full spatial uniqueness and full-sequence weak
convergence of actual window and global vague laws. Different arbitrary
O(1)-rounded actual assignments yield the same actual global limit law.
The window limit realizes every finite disjoint interval/surplus mixed
factorial-density integral.
Actual marked window laws have vanishing total Perron-mark deviation,
all bounded continuous coupled global test means have proved marking
transfer, and marked global laws are tight. Every actual unmarked weak
subsequence converges, after genuine Perron marking, along the same indices;
simultaneous actual unmarked/marked vague weak subsequences are constructed.
Both the actual finite unmarked and empirical-marked window and global
vague laws have unique full-sequence weak limits, with the actual Perron
marking identified. These constructed law limits are not yet identified
with the literal Brownian/Aldous law.
Actual countable finite supports give genuine spectral-critical models;
their canonical Perron functions and moments, embedded mark measures and
literal paper edge hazards agree exactly with the countable constructions.
The actual retained empirical vertex assignment has exactly the empirical
population weights and constructs a spectral-critical finite model at every
index with positive retained counts.
One actual positive-count support sequence simultaneously realizes the
spectral-radius, alpha/beta and embedded Perron-mark total-variation limits,
with the paper's scaled minimum population condition and exact populations.
The actual finite starred window and global laws also have unique
full-sequence limits: size is multiplied by beta^(1/3), surplus and
actual empirical marks are unchanged, and the factorial-density Jacobian
and alpha*beta^(-2/3)*lambda parameter match exactly. The actual countable
component marks equal the pushforward of the actual retained finite marks
as whole probability measures, and their variation distance is the literal
atomic absolute variation. Varying critical parameters converging to lambda
also have the actual raw-time full-window marked/unmarked factorial limits,
including arbitrary rounded counts, floors and diverging size subsequences.
The actual countable normalized independent-edge law equals its empirical critical finite-model
law, and the unnormalized law equals the normalized law at the actual
effective parameter.
The finite weak probability marks embed continuously into the literal
countable atomic-variation space, which is proved complete and Polish;
actual coupled TV-mark factorial
limits are proved on each fixed finite support. One positive actual
realization can be chosen to satisfy countably many separately proved
eventual fixed-support refinements; this selection theorem alone is not
a growing-support graph limit. The paper's actual empirical spectral
drift assumption gives the lambda+theta shift at the n+1-vertex indexing.
The actual Brownian pinned bridge has its proved covariance and whole
endpoint independence. Its finite test laws, exact independent-product
endpoint law and genuine exponential tilt measures are also proved.
This does not yet condition the bridge to a positive excursion.
The literal signed continuous bridge area has its proved Gaussian law,
variance T^3/12 and whole endpoint independence, and its true exponential
path tilt has the exact weighted density and Gaussian area law. This is
not the area of a positive excursion. Actual fixed reference truncations
have critical-scale rounding spectral drift tending to zero and an exact
whole-graph reparameterization. Their actual empirical-normalized graph
laws have full-window floor factorial asymptotics, including true natural
type TV marks; retained Perron quantities and marks converge to the
original countable quantities. One actual exhaustive positive count realization
now has the growing-support local factorial formula for the original
alpha/beta density, uniformly on bounded scalar parameters and every fixed
order, surplus range and positive size window. The same realization has
the literal unnormalized local formula at lambda+theta whenever its actual
empirical spectral roots satisfy the stated critical-scale drift. Actual
TV-marked empirical window laws are genuine continuous finite-mark
pushforwards, with exact whole-law effective-parameter identities. Finite
fixed-assignment TV-marked windows have their proved full-sequence limit,
without assuming compactness of the countable mark space.
The Brownian--Wright density identity and countable
graph-limit terminals are not yet complete. Genuine disjoint
positive-length intervals in a bounded time horizon form a finite family;
the actual Brownian positive-size-window application is proved. Actual
Gaussian fourth moments and growing dyadic chaining give sublinear growth.
On one full source set, simultaneously for every drift and positive cutoff,
all long complete excursion components lie in one finite time horizon and
there are only finitely many. Path-law and reflected-law versions are proved.
The genuine full Brownian size/surplus point-process law is constructed
in the existing vague-Borel point space. Its literal full excursion Dirac
sum agrees almost surely under the original Gaussian joint source;
complete spatial component-cell PPP counts realize the same law. Every
genuine compact window is a measurable finite weak-Borel point process
equal to the global measure restriction. Its Wright factorial density
still requires identification.
Actual complete-excursion tuple weights at every order are derived from
the genuine conditional independent full-area Poisson kernel. Nonnegative
Tonelli gives the literal Brownian source formula without finite-moment
assumptions; the actual compact point-law first moment agrees with its
Campbell area sum. Full bridge area tilt is identified with the actual
deterministic parabolic mean shift as a compact-open continuous path law.
These results do not assert positive-excursion conditioning or Wright
factorial density identification.
Intrinsic rectangle factorials, with overlapping slots and multiplicities,
are now identified with the actual complete-area source integrals in every
order. The actual continuous pinned bridge law is cyclically invariant;
literal minimum-shift geometry and the cyclic area identity are proved.
One actual countable realization also has all window factorial moment
limits, a unique component-number weak limit, point-law tightness and
whole-window TV profile concentration. Its unnormalized window count
parameter is exactly lambda+theta under the actual stated spectral drift.
These count-law conclusions alone do not assert full spatial convergence.
The new literal weighted-cell integration, joint cell-count moment
construction, boundary estimates and rational generating family now prove
unique full-sequence actual growing-support spatial window limits. The
same realization supplies normalized windows and unnormalized windows at
lambda+theta. Actual empirical TV-marked bounded tests approach the true
constant-Perron pushforwards; joint weak subsequences are constructed
without assuming compactness of the mark space. Intrinsic arbitrary Borel
coupled factorial tests retain all atom multiplicities and equal the true
complete-excursion Poisson source integrals. The measurable actual least
bridge minimum, its genuine minimum-shift law and area are constructed;
the actual Brownian bridge has a strictly negative interior minimum
almost surely, using proved cyclic invariance and diffuse Gaussian
increments. Actual growing countable graph laws now have unique full
global unmarked vague limits and full-sequence localized TV-marked
window limits, with canonical original Perron marking. Under actual
critical-scale spectral drift, both statements hold for the same raw
integer graph source at lambda+theta. Literal Brownian--Wright
identification is still required. Actual bridge minimum uniqueness and
strict interior positivity of its genuine minimum-shift law are now
proved from whole-path Gaussian regression and separated minima. This
does not identify the minimum-shift law with a conditioned excursion.
Its actual area is strictly positive almost surely. The genuine Borel
first-downcrossing time is attained when finite; finite-horizon survival
and endpoint probabilities have exact actual pinned-bridge/Gaussian
integrals. Negative full linear Brownian drift gives finite first
passage for every level, using proved full-horizon sublinear growth.
The countable original beta^(1/3) global normalization is also an exact
proper size dilation of the true finite graph source and its full limit.
The same growing integer realization supplies the literal beta^(1/3)
localized TV-marked window laws. Actual Brownian bridge dilation scales
the genuine minimum-shift area by T^(3/2), without an excursion-area
or Wright-constant identity as a premise.
The true bridge minimum-time/minimum-shift joint law is invariant under
cyclic offsets. A proved monotonicity argument upgrades a Gaussian-a.e.
continuous formula for actual pinned survival to every endpoint.
Actual Brownian path reflection at the first downcrossing capped at any
finite horizon now preserves its full path law, by proved finite-grid
fiber invariance and locally uniform path convergence. No strong-Markov
or reflection interface is assumed.
The reflected Gaussian density ratio, its restricted Radon--Nikodym
identity, and the continuous bounded candidate survival factor are
proved by literal Gaussian algebra. These identities alone are not
called the killed Brownian kernel.
The actual killed endpoint measure is now proved to have that literal
Gaussian difference density. Genuine pinned bridge survival probabilities
are identified at every endpoint, including the true zero-endpoint
normalization, from reflection and density uniqueness followed by the
proved monotone pointwise upgrade.
Actual minimum-time uniformity and independence of the entire shifted
path are proved by full circle Haar product factorization and literal
interval unwrapping, under both Brownian and pinned bridge laws. Exact
bridge minimum tails give every exponential moment of the true shifted
area without assuming independence of area and minimum. Its actual first
moment and normalized second moment equal the unchanged Wright constants
at surplus one and two. Genuine killed transition kernels have a proved
deterministic-time semigroup identity and a true surviving two-endpoint
joint kernel decomposition, derived from whole past/future independence.
Arbitrary finite surviving endpoint tuples, including repeated ordered
times and all intermediate coordinates, have the actual iterated killed
kernel law. Positive-start killed densities and their boundary entrance
limits are proved from the true path law. Positive-endpoint conditioned
bridges have their actual normalization and strict positivity, without
declaring an excursion limit. Literal path-area addition gives the actual
area-weighted finite kernel semigroup from whole independent segments.
Joint duration/state measurability and the literal area-weight integral
calculus are proved by finite quadratures and the fundamental theorem.
All cubic
configuration compensation coefficients have a proved factorial formula;
the genuine first connected coefficient gives unchanged Wright constant
two equal to 5/24. Actual root-component half-edge decomposition, its
label-subset size grouping, and the complete nonlinear recurrence for
the unchanged literal connected compensation sum are proved. The exact
Gamma normalization is the unchanged Wright constant. All-order area identity,
excursion conditioning, actual Palm deletion and full Brownian--Wright
factorial densities remain obligations. The actual finite strictly ordered
free endpoint tuple now has its literal Gaussian-difference product density.
The genuine positive bridge has a proved full one-point density and bounded
window entrance/exit limits. All-order Kac insertion for actual surviving
area-power measures and Duhamel insertion for the actual exponential kernel
are derived from literal path calculus, Tonelli and whole-segment independence.
Every actual killed-area moment law is now proved finite, with its literal
Gaussian-insertion density, signed Kac formula, exact Brownian scaling and
all-order Laplace Taylor remainder. The actual positive bridge has arbitrary
ordered-coordinate density limits on the full state space: the entrance
product has mass one, every bounded Borel coupled test converges, and the
literal density L1 error tends to zero. Uniform interior fourth increments
and the common interior Kolmogorov condition are proved. Actual all-time
coordinate and all-order area moments are uniformly bounded near zero
endpoint, and every area-power tail vanishes uniformly. The complete
conditioned path law and its actual area law have exact Brownian duration
scaling. Genuine internal finite laws have proved deletion consistency
and a constructed countable-coordinate probability realization, with
zero limiting endpoints. Actual full-interval fourth increments include
both endpoints. A generic fourth-moment-to-dyadic-modulus theorem and
literal compact path good sets are proved, without regularity premises.
Actual finite-coordinate polynomial moments converge without inserted
uniform-integrability or target-moment assumptions. The entrance sample
law has a constructed continuous Path probability realization matching
its complete countable sampling law, with zero endpoints and stopped
portion. Its moment and continuity inputs have all been discharged from
genuine source kernels. The actual small-positive-endpoint bridge family
is tight in the true continuous Path space, with one common endpoint
neighborhood and genuinely compact sets for every error tolerance.
The genuine directed full-path conditioning limit is now proved by actual
tightness, weak-cluster finite laws and measurable stopped-path sampling
uniqueness. Every actual positive-bridge area moment converges to the
literal entrance-kernel time-cube integral, whose finiteness is proved.
The genuine minimum selector is continuous at unique minima, and the
actual Brownian minimum-shift map is almost surely continuous.
The continuous entrance law now has its actual arbitrary-time Borel
finite-coordinate formulas and full ordered entrance densities. Every
area moment of this true law is identified with its finite entrance-kernel
integral, and the complete entrance path and area laws have exact duration
scaling. The actual bounded first-passage whole-future law is Brownian
and independent of the true passage time and stopped past.
Actual zero-drift first passage to a negative level is now almost surely
finite, positive and hits the level exactly. Its full uncapped past/future
product law has no extra finiteness or strong-Markov premise. The actual
positive-bridge minimum shift is exactly a normalized low-height occupation
bias of the true minimum-shift law. The actual pinned bridge conditioned
on a small positive minimum time converges to that minimum-shift law;
this is not identified with barrier conditioning. Actual killed area
moment duration resolvents satisfy the genuine height-insertion recurrence
and exact Borel endpoint-test transforms. The true entrance-area duration
transform has its finite Gamma normalization at every positive order.
The actual negative-level passage now has its complete Borel density,
exact Laplace transform and successive-depth time-law convolution.
Finite-time reversal preserves the entire Brownian path law and proves
that the actual earliest minimum is strictly interior. Actual minimum
depth-window disintegration retains the whole future path; its literal
negative-level average converges to the true minimum-time/level/future
law, without a minimum-law or distributional-limit premise. Normalized
survival mass provides a proved integrable endpoint-time majorant.
The genuine zeroth killed-area duration transform has its exact Green
formula. Actual all-order symmetry, finite total state mass and the
weighted Green bound prove pointwise finiteness at every order. The
actual initial-state boundary slope passes through each Kac insertion
by proved dominated convergence. True state-mass polynomial bounds give
finite exponentially weighted state integrals at every order.
Actual killed one-boundary finite-coordinate laws have global entrance
limits for joint bounded continuous tests, including literal unshifted
path coordinates and terminal survival. Minimum-window convergence also
has its exact nonnegative whole-future density representation. Genuine
Green integrals on exponentially weighted polynomials are evaluated at
every degree, and actual all-order resolvent boundary responses are
identified with literal polynomials satisfying the proved differential
equation and zero-boundary condition.
Their normalized formal boundary series has a derived Riccati equation
and a proved transport identity by polynomial uniqueness. The actual
Brownian minimum-time/level/terminal-displacement joint density is now
identified by genuine depth and time dominated convergence and uniqueness
of the two actual window limits. The true level-weighted passage density
integrates to one half. Actual time-cube sorting has its factorial
integral identity, and cumulative positive gaps preserve Lebesgue measure
and give precisely the positive strictly ordered time vectors.
Minimum-shift/excursion identification, the full Wright area identity and
the Aldous/Palm factorial-density identity remain obligations.
-/
